<Window x:Class="DCST4.HelpWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Width="680"
        Height="640"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner">
    <FlowDocumentScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
        <FlowDocument FontFamily="Segoe UI" FontSize="13" PagePadding="20" TextAlignment="Left">
            <FlowDocument.Resources>
                <Style x:Key="H" TargetType="Paragraph">
                    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16"/>
                    <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
                    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF1F3A5F"/>
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,14,0,4"/>
                </Style>
            </FlowDocument.Resources>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Quick start</Paragraph>
            <List>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Enter the server's AE title, host and port under Server. Try Ping and Dicom Echo.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Under Exam, select the modality (CT, MR, CR, DX or US) and exam type, and how many images you want. 1 series with 1 image gives a single test image.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Click Generate &amp; Send, and follow each image in the Results tab.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                <ListItem><Paragraph>Compare the text burned into the image with the tags shown in the PACS viewer.</Paragraph></ListItem>
            </List>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Auto and manual values</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Everything on the Identifiers tab is generated by default, and the fields show what the next run will use. Untick Auto to enter your own value. Auto values are drawn when the program starts and when you click New values, and they stay on screen after a run so you can look the exam up in PACS. The values a run used are also written to the Log tab.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Running again without New values uses the same patient, accession number and Study UID, so the images arrive as a new series in the same study, also if you changed modality or exam type. Series numbers start at 1 again, and an Auto Study Date/Time is the time of each run. Click New values to start a separate study. To draw new values after every run instead, tick Draw new Auto values after each run under File &gt; Settings.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>A manual Series UID requires exactly one series, and a manual SOP Instance UID exactly one image, because these must be unique.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Additional tags</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Under File &gt; Settings, on the Additional tags tab, you can add tags on top of the fixed fields. Each one gets a row on the Identifiers tab, where you can untick Auto and type a value for the session.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Common tags are ticked in a list, and Auto generates their values. A custom tag is entered as (0008,1070), 00081070 or a keyword such as OperatorsName, and Auto uses the default value you enter. An empty default sends the tag empty. Separate several values with a backslash where the tag allows it.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>A private tag, one with an odd group number, also needs a private creator and a VR. A custom tag can replace a generated value such as Manufacturer, but not one that would break the image or remove its marking as a test image. The message says why when a tag cannot be added.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Patient IDs</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Random Patient IDs only ever come from Skatteverket's official list of test personnummer, built into the program. Birth date and sex are taken from the number. The list also holds future dates and people born in the 1890s, so random selection is limited to the age range below the fields, 0 to 100 by default.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If you enter a Patient ID that is not on the list, the program warns you. It is still used, but make sure it is not a real person's number.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Names with å, ä, ö</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>About 40% of random names contain å, ä or ö. Select the Specific Character Set under Exam: ISO_IR 100 (Latin-1) or ISO_IR 192 (UTF-8). A manual value that ISO_IR 100 cannot represent stops the run with a message, rather than being sent wrong.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If the viewer shows Ã¥ instead of å, the system has read UTF-8 text as Latin-1. The image text next to it shows what was intended.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Transfer syntax and fallback</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The images are sent in the selected transfer syntax. fo-dicom also always proposes Implicit VR in a presentation context of its own, as DICOM expects. Each context is shown in the Log tab with the server's answer.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>If the server does not accept the selected syntax, the run stops with an error and nothing is sent, so a test of JPEG Lossless can not pass by accident. Tick Allow fallback to Implicit VR to send as Implicit VR instead, as a real modality would. The run then finishes with a warning, and the Syntax used column shows what was really sent.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Reading the results</Paragraph>
            <Table CellSpacing="4">
                <Table.Columns>
                    <TableColumn Width="110"/>
                    <TableColumn/>
                </Table.Columns>
                <TableRowGroup>
                    <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph>Success</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Status 0x0000. The server has taken responsibility for the image.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFFF4C2"><TableCell><Paragraph>Warning</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Stored, but the server changed or dropped something. For example 0xB000 coercion, 0xB006 elements discarded, 0xB007 data set does not match the SOP class.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFFAD4D0"><TableCell><Paragraph>Failure</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Not stored. For example 0xA7xx out of resources, 0xA9xx data set does not match, 0xCxxx cannot understand. The run continues with the next image.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    <TableRow Background="#FFE6E6E6"><TableCell><Paragraph>NotSent</Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>No response for this image, for example because the association was rejected, aborted or timed out. The description says why.</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                </TableRowGroup>
            </Table>
            <Paragraph>Vendor-specific codes keep their real value in the Status column. The status bar shows the totals and throughput of the last run. Images never generated because the run stopped early have no row, but are counted as not sent in the totals.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Saving to disk</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Tick Save to disk, with or without Send to server. The folder becomes a DICOM File-set that viewers can open: a DICOMDIR at the top, and the images in DICOM\EX000001\S001\IM0001 in the selected transfer syntax. DICOM limits these names to 8 characters and no extension, so the folders do not show patient details. The Saved to column shows where each image went.</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Each run gets a new EX folder and nothing is overwritten. Saving again to the same folder adds to the same DICOMDIR. Each file is saved before it is sent, so it exists even if sending fails, and the DICOMDIR is written when the run ends, also if it stopped early.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Version check</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>Opening Help &gt; About asks GitHub for the latest release and shows the result in the window, with a link if there is a new version. Nothing is downloaded or installed. If GitHub cannot be reached, for example on a closed network, the window says so and the program carries on.</Paragraph>

            <Paragraph Style="{StaticResource H}">Logs and settings</Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>The Log tab shows this program's messages, and the complete log is in File &gt; Open log directory (%LocalAppData%\DCST4\Logs). Settings are stored in %LocalAppData%\DCST4\user.config.</Paragraph>
        </FlowDocument>
    </FlowDocumentScrollViewer>
</Window>
